  <div class="section-title">Academic Integrity</div>
  <p><span data-field="academic_integrity_text">Your commitment, as a student, to learning is evidenced by your enrollment at San Jose State University. The <a href="{{ academic_integrity_policy_link }}">{{ academic_integrity_policy_link_text }}</a> at <a href="{{ academic_integrity_policy_url }}">{{ academic_integrity_policy_url_text }}</a> pdf requires you to be honest in all your academic course work. Faculty members are required to report all infractions to the office of Student Conduct and Ethical Development. The <a href="{{ student_conduct_link }}">{{ student_conduct_link_text }}</a> is available at <a href="{{ student_conduct_url }}">{{ student_conduct_url_text }}</a>.</span></p>

  <div class="section-title">Campus Policy in Compliance with the American Disabilities Act</div>
  <p><span data-field="disabilities_act_text">If you need course adaptations or accommodations because of a disability, or if you need to make special arrangements in the building must be evacuated, please make an appointment with me as soon as possible, or see me during office hours. <a href="{{ presidential_directive_link }}">{{ presidential_directive_link_text }}</a> at <a href="{{ presidential_directive_url }}">{{ presidential_directive_url_text }}</a> pdf requires that students with disabilities requesting accommodations must register with the <a href="{{ accessible_education_center_link }}">{{ accessible_education_center_link_text }}</a> (AEC) at <a href="{{ accessible_education_center_url }}">{{ accessible_education_center_url_text }}</a> to establish a record of their disability.</span></p>

